{
 "why": "Which way each team stat ranks, on both apps. team_stats.py and TeamStatCatalog.swift each hold lowIsGood, the team's own stats where less is better; the opponent's version of a stat goes the other way. countsOfTries read highest first for a team and its opponents alike, as does games played. catalog is every stat the iPhone's league list shows, in its order. beyondTheCatalog is a few the Windows list and the iPhone's Team Hub rank as well. rankGrid is how a column of numbers becomes ranks: teams level share a rank, and the next rank counts them. knownStats is every column ESPN has given, by sport, and the validator warns about one that isn't here. tests/unit/test_team_stats.py holds Windows to this and TeamStatsTests.swift the iPhone. A change to any of it but knownStats is a change to both apps.",
